  {
   "id": "XNteYbzeAwAJ",
   "from": "Helpdesk (Haavard Rue)",
   "author": "3eab71733027a24a",
   "date": "2024-08-08T05:37:55Z",
   "subject": "Re: [r-inla] How to set same hyperparameters for two copy features",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div><div><br></div><div>yes, </div><div><br></div><div>you can say the scaling parameter in a copy to be eq to another one, so</div><div><br></div><div>f(sz, copy=&quot;se&quot;, replicate=sz.repl, fixed=FALSE , hyper=hypercopy)+</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div style=\"color:rgb(61,61,61);font-family:&quot;Noto Sans&quot;;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">f(sz0, copy=“se0”, fixed=FALSE, hyper=hypercopy) +</div><br></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>can be replaced with</div><div><br></div><div>f(sz, copy=&quot;se&quot;, <a href=\"http://same.as\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://same.as&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434999065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw048vIBzpxHqOj6KdKPLJW6\">same.as</a>= &quot;sz0&quot;, replicate=sz.repl, fixed=FALSE , hyper=hypercopy)+</div><div style=\"color:rgb(61,61,61);font-family:&quot;Noto Sans&quot;;font-style:normal;font-variant-caps:normal;font-weight:400;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;text-decoration:none\">f(sz0, copy=“se0”,<span> </span><b><a href=\"http://same.as\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://same.as&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792434999065000&amp;usg=AOvVaw048vIBzpxHqOj6KdKPLJW6\">same.as</a>=&quot;sz&quot;,</b><span> </span>fixed=FALSE, hyper=hypercopy) +</div><br><div>sa</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><div>On Tue, 2024-08-06 at 20:56 -0700, Ruby Ji wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><blockquote type=\"cite\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:2px #729fcf solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>Dear all,</div><div><br></div><div>I am developing a joint model with two copied spatial field. I am wondering if it is possible to specify same hyperparameters for sz0 and sz. The model form is:</div><div><br></div><div>form &lt;- y ~ 0 + e.b0 + z.b0 + </div><div>f（se0, model=spde) +</div><div>  f(se, model=spde, replicate=se.repl) +</div><div>  f(sz0, copy=“se0”, fixed=FALSE, hyper=hypercopy) +</div><div>  f(sz, copy=&quot;se&quot;, replicate=sz.repl, fixed=FALSE , hyper=hypercopy) </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Ruby</div><div> </div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
